Package: mbtools
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: League-Microbit mbtools <https://github.com/League-Microbit/mbtools/issues>
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_KB@
Depends: libc6, libusb-1.0-0, udev
Recommends: systemd
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/League-Microbit/mbtools
Description: find, flash and talk to BBC micro:bits across a fleet of hosts
 mbregistry is the per-host daemon that watches USB for micro:bits,
 identifies them, grants exclusive locks, and peers with other hosts over
 mDNS/ZeroMQ. mbdeploy, mbserial and mbrelay are its clients.
 .
 Self-contained: bundles its own Python under /usr/lib/mbtools. Installs
 and starts mbregistry.service (as root) and a udev rule for the micro:bit
 DAPLink interface.
